This document lists the steps required to build an Ubuntu 16-04.4 server prod-01 to run ODL containers using Docker
We will prep the server, set up a docker environment and  create  ODL docker images.

## Install Ubuntu 16.04-04 LTS Server Edition with 4 n/w interfaces - ens32,33,34,36

## set up  host network interfaces  - Add the following config to /etc/network/interfaces

	sudo nano /etc/network/interfaces

	# The primary network interface
	auto ens32
	iface ens32 inet static
		address 172.20.254.220
		netmask 255.255.254.0
		gateway 172.20.254.1
		dns-nameservers 8.8.8.8 8.8.4.4

	# This is peer-to-peer data interface 1
	auto ens33
	iface ens33 inet manual

	# This is peer-to-peer data interface 2
	auto ens34
	iface ens34 inet manual
	#
	auto ens36
	iface ens36 inet manual

## Update packages

	sudo apt-get install
	sudo apt-get update
	sudo apt-get install wireshark wget curl

